    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/cat-harness-minimum.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "issue",
      "cat-harness:section": "(header)",
      "prov:value": "> **Proposal, nothing built.** Answers\n> [#223 comment 16:13](https://github.com/litlfred/folio-assistant/issues/223#issuecomment-5732811137)\n> (minimum contents, Tools strawperson, documentation move-table) as revised by\n> [comment 16:28](https://github.com/litlfred/folio-assistant/issues/223#issuecomment-5732987719)\n> (the harness is **not** self-documenting). Inventory measured on `main` at\n> `d8632b6`, 2026-09-18.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#223 comment 16:13",
        "#223 comment 16:28",
        "d8632b6",
        "2026-09-18"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-18"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/cat-harness-minimum.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The falsifier, stated up front",
      "prov:value": "**Measured below: 17 of 55 `folio-core` skills.** That is a\nreal constraint — it excludes 38 — but it is more than \"a handful\", and §\"What\nI would cut further\" says where I would push if you want it smaller.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "17 of 55 folio-core skills"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/cat-harness-minimum.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Schemas (.ts, minimal)",
      "prov:value": "`TodoItem` already exists at `schemas/types.ts:1330` and carries `id`,\n`summary`, `comment`, `status`, `priority`, `origin`, `targetLabel`,\n`assignee`, timestamps, `updatedBy`, `data`, `related`, `author`. Its\n`TodoStatus` union *already includes `blocked`*. So the Todo half of 16:28's\n\"add if not exists\" is a **move, not a write**.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "schemas/types.ts:1330",
        "src/workflow/bean-link.ts:40"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/cat-harness-minimum.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Skills — 24",
      "prov:value": "> **The count was wrong and is corrected here.** This heading read \"17\" while\n> the table below it listed **19** rows, and named a twentieth — the narrative\n> process skill — as not yet written. That skill now exists as `process-state`,\n> and `skills-and-tools` was added with it, bringing the moved-from-`folio-core`\n> figure to **19 + 2 = 21**. The \"17\" was never recomputed after rows were\n> appended. Three further skills — `mcp-projection`, `mcp-assembly`,\n> `mcp-contract` — are **new writing rather than moves**, for a harness total\n> of **24**. Counted 2026-09-18 with `grep -c` over the table; the grouping\n> below sums to the same number, which is the check that catches the next\n> drift.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-18",
        "count correction"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-18"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/cat-harness-minimum.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Skills — 24",
      "prov:value": "Classified by reading each skill's description, not its filename — the\n[bean `dh4f`](https://github.com/litlfred/folio-assistant/issues/223) lesson.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean dh4f",
        "#223"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/cat-harness-minimum.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "issue",
      "cat-harness:section": "Documentation — the smallest set",
      "prov:value": "- a minimal coding policy ([#243](https://github.com/litlfred/folio-assistant/issues/243));",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#243"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/cat-harness-minimum.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Tools — four nodes, and no MCP",
      "prov:value": "The CLI is absent from a fresh container, and an\nagent that knows only the CLI reads the plan and touches nothing — the\n2026-09-18 failure where a session completed two merged PRs' worth of durable\nwork unclaimed.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-18"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-18"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/cat-harness-minimum.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Carrying it — authored once in Zod, rendered downstream",
      "prov:value": "**Decided (2026-09-18, by the repository owner): the `.ts` Zod schema is\nauthoritative, and as many downstream renderings are generated from it as make\nsense — JSON-LD and JSON Schema to begin with.**",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-18"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-18"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/cat-harness-minimum.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Why not the other three, including the one I first recommended",
      "prov:value": "this\n  repository has just spent a bean (`dzl3`) on a suite that was not running at\n  all, so \"CI will catch it\" is a claim with a poor local record.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean dzl3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/cat-harness-minimum.md#provenance-10",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Why not the other three, including the one I first recommended",
      "prov:value": "An earlier draft of this page recommended authoring the JSON-LD directly, with\nZod validating it in CI. **That is the same two artefacts with the authority\npointing the wrong way**, and the difference is not cosmetic:",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "earlier draft"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/cat-harness-minimum.md#provenance-11",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The documentation move-table",
      "prov:value": "Measured on `main` at `d8632b6`: **18 top-level pages, 8 guides, 20 BPMN\nprocesses, 115 skills across 9 packages.**",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "d8632b6",
        "#232",
        "#243"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/cat-harness-minimum.md#provenance-12",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Decided: 17 stays, and the forge is isolated at the Tool layer",
      "prov:value": "Settled 2026-09-18 by the repository owner. **All 17 skills stay in\n`cat-harness`. There is no sixth repository.**",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-18"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-18"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/cat-harness-minimum.md#provenance-13",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Decided: 17 stays, and the forge is isolated at the Tool layer",
      "prov:value": "**Measured on `main`, 2026-09-18.** The four skills total 1,404 lines.\n`coordinate.md` alone is 731 lines carrying 94 matches for GitHub-ish terms —\nof which **12** are concrete invocations (`mcp__github__*`, `gh pr`, `gh api`)\nand the other 82 are conceptual: \"pull request\", \"PR\", \"GitHub\" as a noun.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-18",
        "1,404 lines"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-18"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/cat-harness-minimum.md#provenance-14",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "The kg/ layout — group them, do not flatten them",
      "prov:value": "The three `mcp-*` skills sit in `bootstrap/` because standing a service up is\nbootstrapping — that is the owner's classification, and it is the right one:\nan agent looking for \"how do I make this tool reachable\" is asking a\nsetup question, not an MCP question.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "owner classification"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/cat-harness-minimum.md#provenance-15",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The kg/ layout — group them, do not flatten them",
      "prov:value": "**The grouping is not implemented here.** This repo is pre-split and its `kg`\nid points at `skills/`, flat. The layout above is the target for\n`cat-harness`, recorded so the split does not land as a flat dump of 17.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "pre-split"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/cat-harness-minimum.md#provenance-16",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "What is deliberately not here",
      "prov:value": "- **The `folio` graph typology is currently mis-sited.** `schemas/cat-harness.ts`\n  lists `folio` among the harness's graph typologies, which contradicts 16:28 —\n  a renderable kind belongs to core. Tracked separately; it is a small\n  correction, not a rewrite.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "schemas/cat-harness.ts",
        "16:28"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/cat-harness-minimum.md#provenance-17",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "What \"renders no content type\" constrains",
      "prov:value": "Cat harness document itself is ok",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "owner, 2026-11-04"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
